// DEXPI 2.0.1: the graph model and sample data
//
// Generated by ../../cypher.py from model.json and sample.json. Edit those and regenerate, rather than this file.
//
// A P&ID extract of the fictional Kestrel Gas Processing Plant, exchanged between engineering tools in the DEXPI
// format. Condensate line 20-113 runs from the feed drum PV-2010 through export pump P-2001A, its discharge valve
// GV-2001 and flow element FE-2001 to an off-page connector. The flow control loop L20.001 senses the segment with an
// orifice measuring system, conveys the signal to controller FIC-2010 and actuates globe valve FV-2001 through a
// fail-close actuator. Duty and standby pumps, with their motors and impellers, sit in the plant's breakdown from
// enterprise to section, area, system and train.
//
// Run it against an empty database of Neo4j 5 or later, Enterprise Edition, for its node key and property existence
// constraints, e.g. with cypher-shell -f model.cypher. It merges every node and relationship, so it can be run again.

// The model: its constraints

CREATE CONSTRAINT id_EngineeringModel_key IF NOT EXISTS FOR (n:EngineeringModel) REQUIRE n.id IS NODE KEY;
